ould build the same surface twice plus an artificial serialization edge. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | E005 | Documentation of the comparison workflow from both entry points. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy provides no Impacted Teams table, no per-component \"what changes\" detail, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no NFRs. Owner teams were derived from the architecture-context files (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/`). Epic acceptance criteria below were derived from the HLRs at a functional level.\n- **Ambiguous role of Data Science Pipelines**: the strategy lists Data Science Pipelines as affected but does not state what changes. It is treated as an active component (E001: run-data retrieval support for multi-run comparison) because pipeline-run parameters and metrics live in the DSP backend that the Dashboard consumes (per `data-science-pipelines.md`). If per-run APIs already in place prove sufficient for comparison retrieval, E001 collapses to validation acceptance criteria on the Dashboard comparison epic and the DAG shortens.\n- **\"Training runs\" provenance unspecified**: the strategy compares \"training and pipeline runs\" but the affected components do not include the Training Operator or a metadata store beyond Data Science Pipelines. E001's scope is written at the functional level (run kinds surfaced in the platform's runs list) to avoid inventing a training-run data source; the implementing teams resolve where training-run parameters and metrics are read from.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\nin-platform.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26355,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-902b41930cbfa34a","agent_id":"ae2a82049772bf047","sessio