{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-271a8d5c-8db7-483f-a89e-ca4611238409","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8464752aab23c0a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-qq52ziw1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Run parameters and metrics retrieval for multi-run comparison (Data Science Pipelines backend)\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the Data Science Pipelines backend support that makes run\nparameters and metrics retrievable for a selected set of runs, in a form the\nDashboard can consume to render multi-run comparisons. Today run parameters and\nmetrics are only accessible through per-run pages; comparing runs requires\nexporting to spreadsheets. This epic provides the run-data foundation for the\nplatform's experiment comparison capability.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the Data Science Pipelines run-data surfaces so that parameters and\n  metrics for a user-selected set of runs can be retrieved together, covering\n  the run kinds surfaced in the platform's runs list (training and pipeline\n  runs).\n- Keep retrieval consistent with the existing per-run parameter and metric data\n  already shown in run detail pages — no changes to how parameters and metrics\n  are recorded, only how they can be retrieved for comparison.\n- Preserve backward compatibility: existing per-run retrieval behavior and the\n  DataSciencePipelinesApplication deployment model are unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a set of two or more runs selected in the platform, their parameters\n  and metrics can be retrieved together through the Data Science Pipelines\n  run-data surface in a single logical operation suitable for side-by-side\n  rendering.\n- The retrieval returns consistent parameter and metric data for runs that\n  declare different sets of parameters and metrics (missing values are\n  representable, not errors).\n- Existing per-run retrieval and run detail behavior is unchanged (no\n  regression to current run pages).\n- The capability is available for the run kinds the Dashboard's runs list\n  surfaces today.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): Users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and\n  metrics side by side in the Dashboard — this epic provides the backend\n  run-data retrieval that the Dashboard comparison view renders.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28337,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-902b41930cbfa34a","agent_id":"ae2a82049772bf047","session_id":"7aaf2973-039f-4d2c-a2b4-8fdd3349d9cb","uuid":"07849500-483c-4b24-a4d8-2f46eb79c391","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:57:57.217Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
