{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-6b4c59ec-4337-4d18-89cb-c8e655a7baf5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2f479f456009758","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-qq52ziw1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Run selection, side-by-side comparison and diff view in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the experiment comparison user experience in the Dashboard:\nusers select two or more runs and view their parameters and metrics side by\nside, with changed values highlighted when comparing two runs. This replaces\nthe exported-spreadsheet workflow data scientists use today to compare training\nand pipeline runs, giving model promotion decisions side-by-side visibility\ninto what changed between candidate runs.\n\n## Description of relationship to platform data\n\nThe comparison view renders run parameters and metrics retrieved through the\nData Science Pipelines run-data retrieval capability for multi-run comparison\n(delivered by the platform's pipelines backend work for this strategy).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add run selection from the Dashboard runs list: users can select two or more\n  runs and open a comparison view.\n- Render selected runs' parameters and metrics side by side, aligned by\n  parameter/metric name.\n- When exactly two runs are compared, highlight which parameters and metrics\n  changed between them (values that differ, added, or missing on either side).\n- Handle runs that declare different sets of parameters and metrics gracefully\n  (missing values shown as such, not as errors).\n- Keep comparison within a single project (no cross-cluster or cross-project\n  comparison, per the strategy's out-of-scope list); no automatic best-run\n  selection or promotion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a runs list, when a user selects two or more runs and opens the\n  comparison, then the selected runs' parameters and metrics are displayed side\n  by side, aligned by name.\n- Given exactly two selected runs, when the comparison is displayed, then\n  parameters and metrics whose values changed between the two runs are\n  highlighted.\n- Given selected runs with differing parameter/metric sets, when the comparison\n  is displayed, then values missing from a run are represented as missing\n  rather than causing an error.\n- The comparison is available from within a single project only; automatic\n  best-run selection and promotion are not part of this capability.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): Users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and\n  metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n- HLR-3 (P1) (bundled with HLR-1): The run \"diff\" view highlighting which\n  parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs is a presentation\n  mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data as HLR-1 — one\n  capability consolidated from two customer councils, delivered by this single\n  epic at the higher priority. Splitting it would build the same surface twice\n  and add an artificial serialization edge.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28956,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-902b41930cbfa34a","agent_id":"ae2a82049772bf047","session_id":"7aaf2973-039f-4d2c-a2b4-8fdd3349d9cb","uuid":"caa39e26-7ab7-4412-9ea4-be2fe62c3648","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:58:07.789Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
