{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-92ca9e86-30ab-4eb3-adb3-d9d5328a34d2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87e5692b9c5b7a37","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-qq52ziw1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E004.md","content":"# Open a run comparison from the Model Registry UI\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the Model Registry user entry point for experiment\ncomparison: from a registered model version in the registry UI, a user can open\na comparison of the run that produced it against other runs. It surfaces the\nrun reference persisted on registered model versions and launches the\nplatform's run comparison capability seeded with that run, so model promotion\ndecisions can start from the registry rather than only from the runs list.\n\n## Scope\n\n- In the Dashboard's Model Registry UI, surface the run reference carried by a\n  registered model version (delivered by the Model Registry run-lineage work in\n  this strategy).\n- Provide an action from a model version that opens the run comparison\n  capability (delivered by the Dashboard comparison work in this strategy)\n  seeded with the producing run.\n- Degrade gracefully for model versions that carry no run reference (no action\n  or a disabled state, not an error).\n- Keep the flow within a single project (no cross-cluster or cross-project\n  comparison, per the strategy's out-of-scope list).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a registered model version that carries a run reference, when a user\n  triggers the compare action in the registry UI, then the run comparison view\n  opens seeded with the producing run so further runs can be selected for\n  side-by-side comparison.\n- Given a registered model version without a run reference, when its detail is\n  viewed, then the UI degrades gracefully with no errors.\n- The registry entry point and the runs-list entry point lead to the same\n  comparison capability (no duplicate comparison surface is built).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P1): Registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n  them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry — this epic\n  delivers the registry-side user entry point that consumes the persisted run\n  reference.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31531,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-902b41930cbfa34a","agent_id":"ae2a82049772bf047","session_id":"7aaf2973-039f-4d2c-a2b4-8fdd3349d9cb","uuid":"cd5d42d2-4cf9-49dc-aa2b-4e45bab8ccc4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:58:37.801Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
