recorded, only how they can be retrieved for comparison.\n50\t- Preserve backward compatibility: existing per-run retrieval behavior and the\n51\t  DataSciencePipelinesApplication deployment model are unaffected.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a set of two or more runs selected in the platform, their parameters\n56\t  and metrics can be retrieved together through the Data Science Pipelines\n57\t  run-data surface in a single logical operation suitable for side-by-side\n58\t  rendering.\n59\t- The retrieval returns consistent parameter and metric data for runs that\n60\t  declare different sets of parameters and metrics (missing values are\n61\t  representable, not errors).\n62\t- Existing per-run retrieval and run detail behavior is unchanged (no\n63\t  regression to current run pages).\n64\t- The capability is available for the run kinds the Dashboard's runs list\n65\t  surfaces today.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): Users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and\n70\t  metrics side by side in the Dashboard — this epic provides the backend\n71\t  run-data retrieval that the Dashboard comparison view renders.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a1655d9cdc6d0af","agent_id":"ac6f01a43f1dcd82d","session_id":"7aaf2973-039f-4d2c-a2b4-8fdd3349d9cb","uuid":"d2c6bd89-9835-4e0e-beba-dc2eacb5a468","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:00:02.125Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98d82edce037082c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
