{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b4462d39ed04806","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Run selection, side-by-side comparison and diff view in the Dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9015-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Run selection, side-by-side comparison and diff view in the Dashboard\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers the experiment comparison user experience in the Dashboard:\n35\tusers select two or more runs and view their parameters and metrics side by\n36\tside, with changed values highlighted when comparing two runs. This replaces\n37\tthe exported-spreadsheet workflow data scientists use today to compare training\n38\tand pipeline runs, giving model promotion decisions side-by-side visibility\n39\tinto what changed between candidate runs. The view renders run parameters and\n40\tmetrics retrieved through the Data Science Pipelines run-data retrieval\n41\tcapability delivered elsewhere in this strategy.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Add run selection from the Dashboard runs list: users can select two or more\n46\t  runs and open a comparison view.\n47\t- Render selected runs' parameters and metrics side by side, aligned by\n48\t  parameter/metric name.\n49\t- When exactly two runs are compared, highlight which parameters and metrics\n50\t  changed between them (values that differ, added, or missing on either side).\n51\t- Handle runs that declare different sets of parameters and metrics gracefully\n52\t  (missing values shown as such, not as errors).\n53\t- Keep comparison within a single project (no cross-cluster or cross-project\n54\t  comparison, per the strategy's out-of-scope list); no automatic best-run\n55\t  selection or promotion.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a runs list, when a user selects two or more runs and opens the\n60\t  comparison, then the selected runs' parameters and metrics are displayed side\n61\t  by side, aligned by name.\n62\t- Given exactly two selected runs, when the comparison is displayed, then\n63\t  parameters and metrics whose values changed between the two runs are\n64\t  highlighted.\n65\t- Given selected runs with differing parameter/metric sets, when the comparison\n66\t  is displayed, then values missing from a run are represented as missing\n67\t  rather than causing an error.\n68\t- The comparison is available from within a single project only; automatic\n69\t  best-run selection and promotion are not part of this capability.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-1 (P0): Users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and\n74\t  metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n75\t- HLR-3 (P1) (bundled with HLR-1): The run \"diff\" view highlighting which\n76\t  parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs is a presentation\n77\t  mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data as HLR-1 — one\n78\t  capability consolidated from two customer councils, delivered by this single\n79\t  epic at the higher priority. Splitting it would build the same surface twice\n80\t  and add an artificial serialization edge.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a1655d9cdc6d0af","agent_id":"ac6f01a43f1dcd82d","session_id":"7aaf2973-039f-4d2c-a2b4-8fdd3349d9cb","uuid":"774aaf19-b76d-4319-aa86-30b5ed39f180","timestam