{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b0dbbf94a0460e2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tscore: 13\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n9\t  description: 'E001 scores open_questions: 1 claiming no unresolved design decision\n10\t    changes the epic approach, but the summary Health Warning records that training-run\n11\t    provenance is unspecified and the implementing teams resolve where training-run\n12\t    parameters and metrics are read from — an unresolved design decision that shapes\n13\t    E001 approach. Re-score open_questions to 0 or -1, or narrow the rationale to\n14\t    the decisions that are resolved.'\n15\terror: null\n16\t---\n17\t## Review Summary\n18\t\n19\tScore: 13/14 — pass\n20\tRecommendation: accept\n21\t\n22\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py RHAISTRAT-9015` exited 0 —\n23\tbody sections, canonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority\n24\tinheritance, implementation-type parallelism, and shared-surface enforcement\n25\tchecks all passed). Triage consistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition)\n26\twith 5 epics — multi-epic output is expected; no contradiction.\n27\t\n28\t## Criterion Details\n29\t\n30\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n31\t\n32\tAll four HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 (P0) → E001 + E002; HLR-2 (P1) → E003 + E004;\n33\tHLR-3 (P1) → E002 (bundled); HLR-4 (P2) → E005. Traceability matrix present in\n34\tthe summary and per-epic HLR Traceability sections exist in every epic file.\n35\t\n36\tHLR-3 bundling into E002 is compliant, not priority collapse: HLR-1 and HLR-3\n37\tdescribe one comparison surface (side-by-side view vs. diff highlighting of the\n38\tsame parameters/metrics over the same run data), the strategy itself notes the\n39\trequirements were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping\n40\twording, and the matrix row carries the `(bundled with HLR-1)` flag plus inline\n41\trationale — satisfying the bundling-recording contract. Splitting them would be\n42\tthe boundary violation (two presentation modes of one surface in two epics).\n43\t\n44\tPriority inheritance is clean: E001 (P0) blocks E002 (P0) — no inversion; E003\n45\t(P1) blocks only P1 work (E004) and the exempt docs epic; no lower-priority epic\n46\tblocks P0 work. E005's P1 priority follows the docs-authoring exception\n47\t(strategy priority Major → P1), correctly not pushed upstream.\n48\t\n49\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n50\t\n51\tNo circular dependencies; every edge references an existing epic. Frontmatter\n52\t`dependencies` match the summary DAG diagram exactly, edge for edge, in both\n53\tdirections (E002: [E001]; E004: [E002, E003]; E005: [E001, E002, E003, E004];\n54\tE001, E003: []), and all arrows run dependency → dependent per the `graph TD`\n55\tconvention. Each edge is justified under the construction rules: E001 → E002 is\n56\ta Rule 13 API-producer → consumer edge (Dashboard code builds against the DSP\n57\trun-data retrieval capability — a genuine build-against artifact, not a\n58\tconfiguration reference); E002 → E004 and E003 → E004 are consumer edges against\n59\tcapabilities/data the upstream epics produce; the four edges into E005 satisfy\n60\tRule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by every Implementation epic).\n61\t\n62\tParallelism is respected: E001 and E003 (different components, different repos,\n63\tno shared artifacts) have no edge between them. No konflux-onboarding,\n64\tlicense-validation, or repo-onboarding epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 are not in\n65\tplay. Cross-checking epic content against the DAG found no uncaptured\n66\tdata/artifact dependencies: every consumed capability (E002's use of E001's\n67\tretrieval, E004's use of E003's run reference and E002's comparison surface,\n68\tE005's coverage of all four implementations) has its edge. Critical path length\n69\t4 (E001 → E002 → E004 → E005) matches the M-strategy heuristic (3-4) and the\n70\tsummary's recorded `critical_path_length: 4`. No conditional branch files exist,\n71\tand none are needed (no bounded outcomes; strategy declares no open questions).\n72\t\n73\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n74\t\n75\tEach epic is a single component/team tuple: E001 (Data Science Pipelines /\n76\tRHOAI Pipelines), E002 and E004 (Dashboard / RHOAI Dashboard), E003 (Model\n77\tRegistry / Model Registry), E005 (Documentation / RHOAI Documentation). E002 and\n78\tE004 share a component and team but are different logical changes on different\n79\tsurfaces — E002 builds the comparison view from the runs list (P0, HLR-1/3);\n80\tE004 adds a registry-side entry point on the model-version detail view,\n81\tconsuming E003's cross-team Model Registry data (P1, HLR-2). The split is\n82\trequired, not a defect: bundling them would serialize the P0 comparison view\n83\tbehind Model Registry work. It is also not scope duplication — E004 explicitly\n84\tdoes not rebuild the comparison surface (its AC: \"no duplicate comparison\n85\tsurface is built\"). No epic mixes code implementation with content authoring\n86\t(docs are the dedicated E005). No epic approaches the ~2-week guideline; no\n87\tenforcement-deliverable extraction exists. Component names are canonical and\n88\tvalidator-confirmed.\n89\t\n90\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n91\t\n92\tAll five epics are Implementation, and each produces a concrete artifact\n93\t(retrieval API capability, Dashboard comparison view, persisted run-reference\n94\tmetadata, registry UI entry point, published documentation). No epic is typed\n95\tInvestigation, and none needs to be: the strategy declares no open questions,\n96\tand the two ambiguities the decomposer identified (DSP's exact role,\n97\ttraining-run provenance) were handled by writing E001's scope at the functional\n98\tlevel with the collapse condition recorded in Health Warnings, rather than by\n99\tinventing a gate. `