{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b03e8fde813e1533","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E001\n3\ttitle: Run parameters and metrics retrieval for multi-run comparison (Data Science\n4\t  Pipelines backend)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n6\tcomponent: Data Science Pipelines\n7\tteam: RHOAI Pipelines\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: -1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Run parameters and metrics retrieval for multi-run comparison (Data Science Pipelines backend)\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers the Data Science Pipelines backend support that makes run\n35\tparameters and metrics retrievable for a selected set of runs, in a form the\n36\tDashboard can consume to render multi-run comparisons. Today run parameters and\n37\tmetrics are only accessible through per-run pages; comparing runs requires\n38\texporting to spreadsheets. This epic provides the run-data foundation for the\n39\tplatform's experiment comparison capability.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Extend the Data Science Pipelines run-data surfaces so that parameters and\n44\t  metrics for a user-selected set of runs can be retrieved together, covering\n45\t  the run kinds surfaced in the platform's runs list (training and pipeline\n46\t  runs).\n47\t- Keep retrieval consistent with the existing per-run parameter and metric data\n48\t  already shown in run detail pages — no changes to how parameters and metrics\n49\t  are recorded, only how they can be retrieved for comparison.\n50\t- Preserve backward compatibility: existing per-run retrieval behavior and the\n51\t  DataSciencePipelinesApplication deployment model are unaffected.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a set of two or more runs selected in the platform, their parameters\n56\t  and metrics can be retrieved together through the Data Science Pipelines\n57\t  run-data surface in a single logical operation suitable for side-by-side\n58\t  rendering.\n59\t- The retrieval returns consistent parameter and metric data for runs that\n60\t  declare different sets of parameters and metrics (missing values are\n61\t  representable, not errors).\n62\t- Existing per-run retrieval and run detail behavior is unchanged (no\n63\t  regression to current run pages).\n64\t- The capability is available for the run kinds the Dashboard's runs list\n65\t  surfaces today.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): Users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and\n70\t  metrics side by side in the Dashboard — this epic provides the backend\n71\t  run-data retrieval that the Dashboard comparison view renders.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6711a469140e526","agent_id":"a6563ec306237aad7","session_id":"7aaf2973-039f-4d2c-a2b4-8fdd3349d9cb","uuid":"f988cebd-5384-448c-bbd1-d3510f531fdd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:05:20.137Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b03e8fde813e1533","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9015"}
