{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acdd99a078d8b243","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E003\n3\ttitle: Run lineage link on registered model versions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run lineage link on registered model versions\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the Model Registry capability that links a registered model\n34\tversion back to the run that produced it. Registered model versions become\n35\ttraceable to their originating training or pipeline run, so a comparison can be\n36\topened from the Model Registry. The Model Registry's custom properties on model\n37\tversions are the extension point for attaching this structured metadata.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Enable a registered model version to carry a reference to the run that\n42\t  produced it, using the model-version extension point (custom properties).\n43\t- Make the run reference retrievable through the existing OpenAPI-specified\n44\t  Model Registry REST API surface, extending it only as needed for this\n45\t  metadata.\n46\t- Preserve backward compatibility: existing RegisteredModel / ModelVersion /\n47\t  ModelArtifact entities, custom properties, and API behavior are unaffected\n48\t  for model versions that carry no run reference.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given a registered model version produced by a run, when the run reference is\n53\t  recorded, then the model version persistently carries a retrievable\n54\t  reference identifying the producing run.\n55\t- The run reference is retrievable through the Model Registry REST API for\n56\t  consuming UIs.\n57\t- Model versions without a run reference continue to be created, read, and\n58\t  managed exactly as before (no regression to existing registry behavior).\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-2 (P1): Registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n63\t  them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry — this epic\n64\t  persists and exposes the link; the registry-side user entry point is\n65\t  delivered by the Dashboard registry integration in this strategy.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6711a469140e526","agent_id":"a6563ec306237aad7","session_id":"7aaf2973-039f-4d2c-a2b4-8fdd3349d9cb","uuid":"e6551e25-55af-49d3-86a9-7cfed27598c0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:05:21.446Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-acdd99a078d8b243","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9015"}
